    "Still": {},
    "Still Is Locked": {},
    "Still Pro": {},
    "Still Pro Is Optional": {},
    "Still Pro is active on this device": {},
    "Still can read the event you are in to put names on the people speaking in your recordings. The calendar stays on this device. This is optional: without it, you name speakers yourself, and you can turn it on later in Settings.": {},
    "Still cannot record until you allow the microphone.": {},
    "Still cannot record without the microphone. Turn on Still in Privacy & Security → Microphone, then come back.": {},
    "Still could not connect %@. Try again, or turn the browser off and on.": {},
    "Still could not finish that": {},
    "Still could not open this file. Check that it still exists and that you can read it, then try again.": {},
    "Still could not read any audio in this file. It may be damaged or incomplete.": {},
    "Still could not save its diagnostic journal. Free up some storage, then try again. (%@)": {},
    "Still follows the input chosen in System Settings unless you pick one here. If the microphone you pick is unplugged, Still uses the system input and says so here and in the menu bar. The test shows the input level and records nothing.": {},
    "Still imports audio files such as M4A, MP3, WAV, AIFF and CAF. This file is not one of them.": {},
    "Still is unsure of these words": {},
    "Still keeps a 90-day journal of what it did and what failed, on this device only. It holds event names, versions, and error numbers — never audio, transcripts, names, file paths, or keys.": {},
    "Still keeps it once it looks like a meeting. A short microphone check is thrown away.": {},
    "Still needs the microphone to record you. Everything it hears stays on this device.": {},
    "Still reads the file without changing it and transcribes it on this device.": {},
    "Still remembers a voice only when you turn it on for a named speaker. A remembered voice only suggests a name; you confirm it. Forgetting stops all future suggestions.": {},
    "Still starts recording when an app you allow here joins a call, meaning it uses the microphone and plays sound at the same time. It saves the recording when the app lets go of the microphone, if the call lasted at least 45 seconds, matches a calendar event, or you chose Keep. Shorter checks, like a microphone test, are thrown away. Music and other apps are not recorded. Recording always shows in the menu bar and can be stopped or thrown away at once. For meetings in a browser, use the Still extension below.": {},
    "Still suggests this name when the voice returns in a later meeting. You confirm each time.": {},
    "Still transcribes and stores meetings on this device. It has no account, analytics, or network service.": {},
    "Stop Recording": {},
    "Stop Test": {},
    "Stop and Save": {},
    "Stop the recording to test the microphone.": {},
    "Storage": {},
    "Suggested name from the call: %@": {},
    "Summarize a recording": {},
    "Sync": {},
    "Sync Now": {},
    "Sync is part of Still Pro.": {},
    "Sync sends your recordings to your own iCloud account, encrypted on this device first. Apple stores only ciphertext: no transcript, note, audio, or key ever leaves in readable form. Text and notes arrive on your other devices before the audio finishes.": {},
    "System Audio": {},
    "System Default": {},
    "System Default (%@)": {},
    "Teal": {},
    "Tells apart the people speaking in a recording, on this device, and recognizes voices you have named before.": {},
    "Test Microphone": {},
    "The App Store is unreachable. Recording keeps working.": {},
    "The Still extension tells the app when a meeting on one of these sites starts and ends, and on Google Meet who is speaking. Still then records only the browser that holds the meeting, so music and videos in other apps stay out, and suggests speaker names you can confirm or reject. The extension reads nothing else from the page, and nothing from your Library ever reaches the browser. Turning the extension off leaves manual recording and allowed call apps working as before.": {},
    "The shortcut works while another app is in front. Still never pauses or changes another app's playback; it only tells you when sound might end up in a recording.": {},
    "This choice stays on this device. Recordings outside it do not appear in the library, search, Siri, or the menu bar, and their audio is not downloaded here. With exactly one project chosen, new recordings go into it.": {},
    "This device could not turn the recording into text. The audio is saved, so you can still play it.": {},
    "This file is too long to import. Still imports up to three hours of audio at a time.": {},
    "This recording stays on this device until you confirm its project. Then it syncs to your other devices.": {},
    "Threw away a short %@ check that was not a meeting.": {},
    "Throw Away": {},
    "Title": {},
    "To record the other people on a call, macOS asks you to allow Screen & System Audio Recording. Still records only sound, never your screen.": {},
    "Transcribe on This Device": {},
    "Transcribing on this device": {},
    "Transcript": {},
    "Transcription": {},
    "Translate to %@": {},
    "Try Again": {},
    "Turn on Still in Privacy & Security → Screen & System Audio Recording. Still records only sound, never your screen.": {},
    "Turn on each browser where you installed the Still extension, so the extension can reach the app. Safari needs no setup here.": {},
    "Turn on the lock for your recordings.": {},
    "Turning on sync sends your recordings to your own iCloud account, encrypted on this device first. Apple stores only ciphertext: no transcript, note, audio, or key ever leaves in readable form. Text and notes arrive on your other devices before the audio finishes.": {},
    "Turns speech into accurate text on this device, in English and 24 other European languages.": {},
